22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You need to match the 3D model with the costume first.

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
In the menu bar, find the virtual model and select the virtual model editor.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
In the top of the virtual model editor, find the costume cladding.

25
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
There are two ways to create a costume.

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
First, you can try the Automatic Clothing Tool.

27
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
In the upper right corner, click the Automatic Clothing Tool button.

28
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
You can see that there is a gray version shadow around the model.

29
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Click the Automatic Clothing Tool button at the bottom.

30
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Rotate to see if the red costume cladding around the model is flat.

31
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
In this way, the costume cladding of the model is completed.

32
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
If the costume cladding is not created correctly,

33
